# CRDC Data Hub Automation Framework

## Project Overview

**crdc-dh-automation** is a Katalon Studio–based UI automation framework for the **Cancer Research Data Commons (CRDC) Data Hub**. It uses **Groovy**, **Selenium**, and **Katalon built-in keywords** to automate end-to-end validation of CRDC workflows. Custom keywords extend Katalon where built-in keywords are insufficient.

**Purpose:** Automate CRDC Data Hub UI validation using custom keywords. Compose existing keywords when adding new tests.

---

## Technology Stack

- **Katalon Studio** (9.x) – test authoring and execution
- **Groovy** – scripting language for keywords and test scripts
- **Selenium** – WebDriver for browser automation
- **Python** – OTP generation for Login.gov 2FA (`PythonFiles/CRDC/GenerateOtp.py`)
- **Apache POI** – Excel/TSV reading for test data
- **Jenkins** – CI/CD (see `jenkins/`)

---

## Project Structure

| Path | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `Keywords/utilities/` | Custom Groovy keywords (Login, Pbac, DataSubmissions, WebUIUtils, Utils, etc.) |
| `Scripts/CRDC/` | Groovy scripts executed by Test Cases (one script per test case) |
| `Test Cases/CRDC/` | Katalon test case definitions (link to Scripts) |
| `Object Repository/` | UI locators (`.rs` files with xpath, id, etc.) |
| `Data Files/` | Katalon Data Files (`.dat` – reference Excel/CSV for test data) |
| `InputFiles/CRDC/` | TSV, Excel, metadata used at runtime (e.g. `MetadataData/TC04/`, `MetadataData/PBAC/`) |
| `Profiles/` | Global variables (URL, credentials) – `default.glbl`, `CRDC_STAGE.glbl`, `CRDC_QA.glbl` |
| `Reports/` | Generated validation reports (HTML) |
| `Include/config/` | Logging and other config |

